 "notes": "J-16 example (dark warm branch): deep spine channel, signature mosaic nose, three nested white V whose arms are tapered spikes (12 degrees to the axis, widest end about 10% of the arm length, sharp tip at the centreline) and two staggered lozenge spikes beside them, twin companion lines, wing mosaic with two tint stripes, inner-fin wedge. Node and material names are J-16 specific; adapt charts and scale coordinates for other airframes. Inner fin faces carry a leading-edge mosaic wedge with two signature companion lines (white stays on the wide nested V); outer fins are left free for portraits. Body chart takes only faces with normal y >= 0.3. Check with surface_map.py before and after changes. Revision 10: the V arms were twisted (inner edge offset the wrong way at the top, so each arm rendered as two crossing needles); fixed so every arm widens toward the nose. Revision 11: the V arms are now tapered spikes measured from the author's Mirage 2000 dorsal (the earlier constant-width 16-degree bars read as blunt road arrows), plus staggered lozenge spikes; the echo outline was dropped with them.",
